# Pipeline timestamps (no per-file bloat)

## Single source of truth

Committed normalized data records **pipeline run times** only in:

`packages/data/cache/normalized/meta/pipeline.json`

Update via `writePipelineMeta()` in `packages/data/src/pipeline-meta.ts`.

| Field | Set by |
| ----- | ------ |
| `extractedAt` | `scripts/1-extract/index.ts` |
| `transformedAt` | `scripts/3-transform/index.ts` |
| `cardsMergedAt` | `scripts/3-transform/07-transform-pokemon-cards.ts` |
| `refreshedAt` | `scripts/5-refresh/index.ts` |
| `bulbapediaIllustratorsCatalogAt` | `scripts/3-transform/04-transform-bulbapedia-illustrators.ts` |
| `bulbapediaExpansionsCatalogAt` | `scripts/3-transform/05-transform-bulbapedia-expansions.ts` |
| `competitiveAppliedAt` | `scripts/3-transform/11-apply-competitive.ts` |
| `tcgTypeProfilesAppliedAt` | `scripts/3-transform/08-transform-tcg-type-profile.ts` |
| `illustratorTcgIndexAt` | `scripts/5-refresh/04-refresh-illustrator-tcg-cache.ts` |

## Do not duplicate on every entity file

**Never** add run timestamps to:

- `meta/cards/expansions/{slug}/info.json`
- `meta/cards/illustrators/{slug}/info.json`
- Per-species `species.json`, `cards.json`, `images.json`, etc.
- `meta/illustrators-catalog.json`, `meta/expansions-catalog.json`, `meta/cards/illustrators/index.json`

Forbidden keys on committed normalized files include: `extractedAt`, `transformedAt`, `generatedAt`, `enrichedAt`, `tcgTypeProfileEnrichedAt`.

`stripAllCommittedNormalizedTimestamps()` runs at the start of every `pnpm transform`.

## Where timestamps are allowed

| Location | Purpose |
| ----- | ---- |
| `cache/normalized/meta/pipeline.json` | Global pipeline runs (committed) |
| `cache/extract-manifest.json` | Per-source extract stats (gitignored) |
| `cache/raw/**` | Per-record extract time (gitignored) |

## When editing transform scripts

- Use `readPipelineMeta()` / `resolvePipelineExtractedAt()` for app-facing “when was data built?”
- If you need per-entity freshness, use **content hashes** or bump `schemaVersion`, not `new Date()` on every file.
